# WME Tasks Layer Assist

A Tampermonkey userscript for the Waze Map Editor (works in beta and production).

WME's **Tasks** layer is all on or all off. This script adds a **Task types** group right under it in the
**Map layers** panel, with a checkbox per issue type, so you can show or hide each type on the current screen:

- Update requests
- Map suggestions (existing segments / editor suggestions)

Hidden types are not drawn and cannot be clicked.

## How it works with the Issue Tracker filter

The Issue Tracker filter still decides which issues are *available* (for example, URs open and closed, Map
suggestions open only). The checkboxes only hide a subset of those on the map. The script never changes the
Issue Tracker filter.

## Behavior

- The group has an expand/collapse arrow like the other layer groups. Collapsing it does not change any checkbox.
- Checkbox and collapse state are remembered between sessions (browser `localStorage`, separately for beta and
  production). A new tab starts from the last saved state. Tabs that are already open are not changed when you
  toggle something in another tab, so one tab can show URs while another shows Map suggestions.
- If you switch the Tasks layer off and on again, unchecked types stay hidden.
- Switching a type back on nudges the map about 20 m and back, because WME only redraws that layer's icons
  after a real map move. If you move the map yourself during the nudge, the script leaves it where you put it.
  WME also closes the Map layers panel when the redrawn data arrives; if the panel was open, the script
  reopens it (up to 3 times, within about 20 seconds).

## Not included (yet)

- **New-segment Map suggestions** (Google-sourced): the WME SDK has no layer switch for these, so they cannot be
  hidden separately.
- **Open-only / closed-only** per type: the SDK has no way to filter inside a layer. Use the Issue Tracker filter.
- **Place update requests** and **Map problems**: not in the first version.

## Technical notes

- Uses the WME SDK in `async` mode only. No `W` or OpenLayers internals, so it is not affected by their removal.
- The Task types group is built by cloning an existing native group in the panel at runtime (WME's panel class
  names are hashed and change between builds). If WME's panel markup changes and the group cannot be built, the
  script falls back to two checkboxes in the shared **Userscripts** group of the Map layers panel.

## Install

1. Install [Tampermonkey](https://www.tampermonkey.net/).
2. Open the raw script link: `https://github.com/TxAgBQ/Scripts/raw/refs/heads/main/wme-tasks-layer-assist/WME-Tasks-Layer-Assist.user.js`
3. Click **Install**. Tampermonkey checks this link for updates.

## Version history

- **2026.11.05.01** - First version: Update requests and Map suggestions (existing) checkboxes under Tasks.
